      <h1>Why Does Bitcoin Matter?</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin matters because it combines open participation, independently verifiable rules, scarce digital units, and ownership through cryptographic keys. Those properties can reduce dependence on central intermediaries, but they also shift more responsibility and risk to the people who use the network.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Foundations</li><li>Surface</li><li>Explainer</li><li>9 to 10 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-15</li></ul>
      <p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Preview only. Publication records and confirmed URLs do not exist; all navigation remains inactive.</p>
