    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide002Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide002Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Bitcoin</dt><dd>An open monetary network and asset governed by independently verified consensus rules.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Bitcoin&#39;s purpose</dt><dd>The monetary and technical goals Bitcoin is designed to serve, including scarce digital ownership without a central issuer.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Scarcity</dt><dd>A condition in which the available supply of something is limited relative to possible demand.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Consensus</dt><dd>The shared validation rules independently enforced by Bitcoin nodes.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Self-Custody</dt><dd>Direct control of the keys needed to spend bitcoin.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Full node</dt><dd>Software that independently verifies Bitcoin blocks and transactions against consensus rules.</dd></div></dl></section>
